  "question_text": "<p>Aside from maximum current rating, what two critical specifications must you check to ensure an LDO regulator doesn't fail?</p>",
  "answer_text": "<p>Power Dissipation (Thermal Resistance) and Dropout Voltage.</p>",
  "explanation_text": "<p>Dropout Voltage (V_DO) is the minimum headroom needed between Vin and Vout. Thermal Resistance (θ_JA) is critical because LDOs dissipate excess voltage as heat (P = (Vin - Vout) * I).</p>\n<img src=\"{{image_1}}\" alt=\"Thermal block diagram of an LDO package radiating heat. Shows the equation P_d = (Vin - Vout) * I_load, and thermal resistance (θ_JA) from junction to ambient.\" style=\"max-width:100%;margin:1rem 0;border-radius:6px;\"/>",
  "bonus_question_text": "<p>How can you improve LDO thermals on a PCB?</p>",
  "bonus_answer_text": "<p>Increase the copper pour area connected to the thermal pad and add thermal vias.</p>",
